      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SUBJECT_SUMMARY\n\n## Column Mapping\n- subject key: SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_KEY\n- subject title: SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- department name: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- number of subject offerings: SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_KEY\n- total number of units: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.TOTAL_UNITS\n- total number of enrolled students: SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- 2012 summer term: SUBJECT_OFFERED.TERM_CODE\n- Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program: SUBJECT_SUMMARY.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n\n## Join Keys\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID <-> SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n- SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID <-> SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_ID\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each subject offered in the 2012 summer term by the Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program, provide the subject key, subject title, department name, the number of subject offerings, and the total number of units for those offerings.\n```sql\nSELECT so.SUBJECT_KEY, so.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME, COUNT(so.SUBJECT_KEY) AS offering_count, SUM(sos.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units FROM SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY sos JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED so ON sos.SUBJECT_ID = so.SUBJECT_ID JOIN SUBJECT_SUMMARY ss ON so.SUBJECT_ID = ss.SUBJECT_ID WHERE so.TERM_CODE = '2012SU' AND ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Harvard Cross-Enrollment Prog' GROUP BY so.SUBJECT_KEY, so.SUBJECT_TITLE, ss.DEPARTMENT_NAME;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each subject offered in the 2012 summer term by the Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program, provide the subject key, subject title, department name, the number of subject offerings, the total number of units for those offerings, and the total number of enrolled students in those offerings. Do not return any rounded answers."
